            - paragraph:
              - text: Emscripten’s filesystem is synchronous, so
              - code: tokio::fs
              - text: and
              - code: io-std
              - text: run their operations inline on the calling thread rather than on the blocking pool, in pthreads builds too.
            - paragraph: When the build links WebAssembly JavaScript Promise Integration (JSPI), a wait that would block suspends on the host event loop rather than blocking. This requires Emscripten 6.0.10 or later. Builds without JSPI will spin on timed parks, and panic otherwise.
            - paragraph:
              - text: Suspension requires the current export to have been wrapped with
              - code: WebAssembly.promising
              - text: . A wait from any other activation throws
              - code: WebAssembly.SuspendError
              - text: . That is a foreign exception rather than a Rust panic, so it can’t be caught by
              - code: catch_unwind
